{"type":"text","timestamp":1770324198149,"sessionID":"ses_3d075eb5affeX5x3AwrqzF123N","part":{"id":"prt_c2f8b7fce001LkXtI24DwEit5B","sessionID":"ses_3d075eb5affeX5x3AwrqzF123N","messageID":"msg_c2f8b683c001t0YrZf96TlReJ3","type":"text","text":"I have created a server component page at `app/timestamp/page.tsx` that displays the current server timestamp.\n\nTo ensure the timestamp updates on every request (opting out of static prerendering without using cookies or headers), I used the **Route Segment Config** `export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'`. This is the standard recommended approach for forcing a page to be dynamic.\n\nYou can verify it works by running the server or checking the build output (which I confirmed shows `ƒ /timestamp` as Dynamic).\n\n**File created:** `app/timestamp/page.tsx`\n```tsx\nexport const dynamic = 'force-dynamic';\n\nexport default function TimestampPage() {\n  const timestamp = new Date().toISOString();\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <h1>Current Server Timestamp</h1>\n      <p>The time is: {timestamp}</p>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n```","time":{"start":1770324198148,"end":1770324198148},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}}
